        <div class="report-content">
            <p>The Phase 02 Technical Evaluation is designed to test first-principles thinking rather than rote memorization. The paper is divided into a Common Core section mandatory for all applicants, and a Domain Specific section based on your chosen division.</p>

            <h3>Common Core Syllabus (40 Marks)</h3>
            <p>All candidates will be tested on fundamental physics (kinematics, basic fluid dynamics) and quantitative reasoning. Calculators are permitted, but no programmable devices or smartphones will be allowed in the hall.</p>

            <h3>Domain Specific Sections (60 Marks)</h3>
            <p><strong>Aerodynamics:</strong> Questions will focus on lift/drag equations, structural integrity scenarios, and basic material properties.</p>
            <p><strong>Embedded Systems:</strong> Expect pseudocode evaluation, basic circuit analysis (Kirchhoff's laws, resistor networks), and logic gate problem-solving.</p>
            
            <p>Please arrive at the venue 15 minutes prior to the commencement of the exam. Candidates arriving late will not be granted additional time.</p>
